# App Store release notes

Manual rule — invoke with `@release-notes`.

Turn recent commits into App Store "What's New" copy.

## Process

1. Run `git log --oneline -20` (and `git log <prev-tag>..HEAD` if a tag exists).
2. Group user-visible changes only. Skip internal refactors, CI, Cursor config.
3. Write 3–6 short bullets in the playful dogtor voice (warm, clear, not corporate).
4. Cap at ~400 characters total.

## Template

```
What's New
• <benefit-focused bullet>
• <benefit-focused bullet>
• <benefit-focused bullet>
```

## Example tone

- Good: "Find pediatric pup specialists faster with breed search."
- Bad: "Refactored ProviderStore filteredProviders sort comparator."
